{title: 639 - A Diligent and Grateful Heart}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #639 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 639}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]A diligent [Bb7]and [Eb/Bb]grateful heart
[Bb]Prompts [Eb]me to sing [Gm]Thy [Bb7/Ab]praise.
[Bb7/D]Thy love [Ab]and [Bb]mer [Ab/C]cies [Fm/Ab]from [Cm/G]the [Bb]start
[Eb/Bb]Have blessed [Fm/Ab]me [Cm/G]all [Ab]mydays.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]I thank [Ab]Thee [Bb7]for [Eb/Bb]the [Bb7/Ab]means [Cm/G]to [Eb/Bb]serve
[Bb]With [Eb]talents and [Gm]with [Bb7/Ab]tithes,
[Bb7/D]For sharing [Bb]brings [Ab/C]the [Fm/Ab]utmost [Bb]joy
[Eb/Bb]When lifting [Cm/G]other [Ab]lives.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]My thanks [Ab]I [Bb/F]give [Bb7]you [Eb/Bb]for [Cm/G]stewardship
[Bb]To [Eb]minister [Gm]through [Bb7/Ab]deeds,
[Bb7/D]To serve [Ab]and [Bb]share [Ab/C]with [Fm/Ab]patient [Bb]care
[Eb/Bb]Thy people [Cm/G]in [Ab]their [Eb/G]needs.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm]O Lord, [Ab]I [Bb7]dedicate [Cm/G]my [Eb/Bb]all
[Bb]In [Eb]this response [Gm]to [Bb7/Ab]Thee.
[Bb7/D]Help me [Ab]to [Bb]magnify [Cm/G]this [Bb]call
[Eb/Bb]In deep [Fm/Ab]humility.
{end_of_verse}
